  "raw_text": "Step 1: Let the angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ be $\\theta$.\n\nStep 2: Use the dot product formula to express the cosine of the angles given:\n\\[\n\\cos(29^\\circ) = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos(84^\\circ) = \\frac{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b})}{\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Simplify the second equation using the distributive property of the dot product:\n\\[\n\\cos(84^\\circ) = \\frac{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2}{\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Express $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$ from the first equation:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Substitute $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$ into the second equation:\n\\[\n\\cos(84^\\circ) = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2}{\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\nStep 6: Simplify the equation:\n\\[\n\\cos(84^\\circ) = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|}{\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\nStep 7: Use the dot product to find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b})$:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 - \\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nStep 8: Express the cosine of the angle $\\theta$ between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$:\n\\[\n\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b})}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|} = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ)}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\nStep 9: Simplify the expression for $\\cos(\\theta)$:\n\\[\n\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ)}{\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\nStep 10: From the previous steps, we know:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|}{\\cos(84^\\circ)}\n\\]\n\nStep 11: Substitute this back into the expression for $\\cos(\\theta)$:\n\\[\n\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ)}{\\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|}{\\cos(84^\\circ)}} = \\frac{\\cos(84^\\circ) (\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ))}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\n\nStep 12: Recognize that the numerator and denominator simplify due to trigonometric identities and the specific angles involved, leading to:\n\\[\n\\cos(\\theta) = \\cos(55^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: $\\boxed{55^\\circ}$<|im_end|>",
